view 0.3.0 (marqdo-view)
Marqdo View renders the original Markdown and attaches verified Analysis v3 facts. Running is never implicit: it requires an explicit user action. Export is always a pure read-only operation.

Usage: marqdo-view [OPTIONS] [PATH] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  export  Write a static, read-only HTML site (never executes the document)
  verify  Check CLI/Analysis/source binding only; never executes

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          A `.mq.md` document or a project directory (default: `.`)

Options:
      --marqdo-bin <PATH>
          Development only: explicit path to the frozen `marqdo` binary. Installed Tool Protocol runs get the path from `MARQDO_BIN`

      --host <HOST>
          Loopback host for the Live reader (default 127.0.0.1)
          
          [default: 127.0.0.1]

      --port <PORT>
          Port for the Live reader; `0` lets the OS choose and prints the real URL
          
          [default: 7429]

      --no-open
          Do not open a browser (the full local URL is still printed)

      --run-timeout <RUN_TIMEOUT>
          Wall-clock limit for one explicit run, in seconds (RFC-VIEW-0002 §6.7). The frozen Core receives the same value via `--timeout`
          
          [default: 30]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
